 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "How the falling leaves fall on above,\nThe life that hath passed away away;\nThe woman who alone\nLay sheltered in her maidenhood's day,\nIn the lone, lonely world of beauty;\nBut now that time has ceased to endure,\nShe lay by herself at Sunday.\nThe winds blew softly and softly by\nAnd I saw what she had ago.\nI watched awhile for herself,\nWhen all things seemed to disappear\nAnd every sound was silent",
